WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:04.799
First: an App Service
origin allows traffic

3
00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:07.650
only from the Front Door
backend service tag.

4
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.287
Is it locked to your Front Door?

5
00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:10.825
The answer is b, no.

6
00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:15.034
The tag's addresses are shared
by every Front Door customer,

7
00:00:15.034 --> 00:00:18.900
so check the X Azure F D I D
header too, or use Private Link.

8
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.700
Second: someone changed the live firewall
policy after a draft was created.

9
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.875
What happens when the draft is deployed?

10
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:29.728
The answer is b: the draft
replaces the whole applied policy,

11
00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:33.187
and the live change is lost
unless it's in the draft too.

12
00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:38.160
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
